<.shell title="Icons" current={:icons}>
  <h1>Icons</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Heroicons, the set the app already uses. A small, fixed list: an icon helps people find or
    recognize something, and never replaces the words.
  </p>

  <h2>The set</h2>
  <p>Only these render. To use a new icon, add it to this list with its use first.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="shrink">16</th>
          <th class="shrink">20</th>
          <th class="shrink">24</th>
          <th class="shrink">Name</th>
          <th>Use</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr :for={{name, use} <- icons()}>
          <td><.svg_icon name={name} size={16} /></td>
          <td><.svg_icon name={name} size={20} /></td>
          <td><.svg_icon name={name} size={24} /></td>
          <td class="mono">{name}</td>
          <td>{use}</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Sizes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>16, solid</strong>: beside sm text: breadcrumbs, back links, pagination, small buttons, chips.
    </li>
    <li><strong>20, solid</strong>: beside md text: buttons, banner titles, toasts.</li>
    <li><strong>24, outline</strong>: on its own line, such as warning text.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In use</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="actions">
      <a href="#" class="back-link" style="margin: 0"><.svg_icon name="chevron-left" size={16} />Settings</a>
      <a href="#" class="btn secondary">Open in D4H
      <.svg_icon name="arrow-top-right-on-square" size={16} /></a>
      <button class="btn secondary"><.svg_icon name="arrow-path" size={20} /> Refresh from D4H</button>
      <a href="#" class="btn sm secondary"><.svg_icon name="arrow-down-tray" size={16} />
      Download PDF</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      An icon sits beside words. The only icon without words is the close or remove ×, and it has an <code>aria-label</code>.
    </li>
    <li>At most one icon per button. It leads, except the external-link icon, which trails.</li>
    <li>
      Only the uses listed above. No icons beside headings, in table cells, or for decoration.
    </li>
    <li>Icons take the text color. Banners and toasts color theirs to match.</li>
    <li>
      In the app: <code>&lt;.icon name="hero-chevron-left-micro" /&gt;</code>
      for 16, <code>-mini</code>
      for 20, and no suffix for 24.
    </li>
  </ul>
</.shell>
